  "answer_text": "The latest iPhone lineup currently includes the **iPhone 17, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone Air, and the newest iPhone 17e**. Apple's flagship iPhone lineup includes the iPhone 17e (2026), iPhone 17 (2025), iPhone 17 Pro (2025), iPhone 17 Pro Max (2025), and iPhone Air (2025).\n\nHere are the best places to buy them:\n\n---\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udf4e Apple (apple.com or Apple Store)\nThe most direct option. You can choose two-hour delivery from an Apple Store, free delivery, or easy pickup options. When you buy your new iPhone directly from Apple, you'll get access to Personal Setup \u2014 guided online sessions where a Specialist can walk you through setup and data transfer or focus on features that help you make the most of your iPhone. You can also trade in your current iPhone or Android device and apply any credit toward your purchase.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \ud83d\udcf1 Carrier Stores (T-Mobile, AT&T, Verizon, etc.)\nT-Mobile, for example, carries the full iPhone 17 lineup, including the iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17e, iPhone Air, and iPhone 17. Carriers often offer installment plans and trade-in deals.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \ud83d\uded2 Best Buy\nYou can shop Best Buy for the latest Apple iPhone and accessories, including the newest iPhone models. You can look for trade-in discounts as well as offers made by coverage plans, and you might consider an unlocked iPhone to gain cellular plan coverage flexibility or open-box products for discounted prices.\n\n---\n\n### 4. \ud83d\udce6 Amazon\nAmazon is a great option for both new and refurbished iPhones. For example, a renewed 128GB iPhone 14 Pro starts at $439, while bumping up the storage to 256GB brings the price of a renewed unit to a still-affordable $479.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Quick Tips:\n- If budget is not a concern and you want the absolute best Apple makes, the iPhone 17 Pro Max ships with the A19 Pro chip and a 6.9-inch ProMotion OLED display.\n- The iPhone 17e is Apple's most affordable option at $599, featuring the A19 chip, 256GB of base storage, MagSafe charging, and a 48MP Fusion camera.\n- Apple is also working on new iPhone 18 models that will come out in the fall of 2026, so if you're not in a rush, it may be worth waiting!",
